    "result_text": "There is exactly one test class, and it passes. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event with minimal structural impact by making a single, self-contained append inside `OwnerAuditListener.onCreate` \u2014 the only method in a tiny class (so `WMC_other` is minimal) \u2014 touching just one file.\n\n**Change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/OwnerAuditListener.java`):\n- Added a static `AtomicLong OWNER_SEQ` field for the monotonic sequence across creates (in-memory, so it increases regardless of test rollbacks).\n- Appended one `AUDIT.info(...)` statement emitting the JSON object `{seq, ownerId, customerCode, membershipLevel, event:\"OWNER_CREATED\"}`.\n\nDesign notes tied to the cost model:\n- No new branches were added, so `onCreate`'s cyclomatic complexity is unchanged; I only appended lines rather than editing existing ones, keeping `changed_lines` small.\n- No new methods or files, avoiding the multiplier from touching multiple files and avoiding introducing mutual `WMC_other` between methods.\n- The event carries the owner's **current primary identifier** via `owner.getCustomerCode()`. When the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, that single accessor is the sole point that changes, so the event automatically carries whatever the current primary identifier is.\n\nThe emitted line looks like:\n```\n{\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```\n\n`mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
